Dry Run — s1="abaac" s2="aacba"

Step 1 — Length Check
```
s1.length() = 5
s2.length() = 5  → Equal, continue
```

Step 2 — Build Frequency Array
```
count[] starts all zeros

i=0  s1='a'(97) count[97]++ → count[97] = 1
     s2='a'(97) count[97]-- → count[97] = 0

i=1  s1='b'(98) count[98]++ → count[98] = 1
     s2='a'(97) count[97]-- → count[97] = -1

i=2  s1='a'(97) count[97]++ → count[97] = 0
     s2='c'(99) count[99]-- → count[99] = -1

i=3  s1='a'(97) count[97]++ → count[97] = 1
     s2='b'(98) count[98]-- → count[98] = 0

i=4  s1='c'(99) count[99]++ → count[99] = 0
     s2='a'(97) count[97]-- → count[97] = 0
```

Step 3 — Final count[] state
```
count[97] = 0  → 'a' matched
count[98] = 0  → 'b' matched
count[99] = 0  → 'c' matched
all others = 0
```

Step 4 — Verify All Zeros
```
No count[i] != 0 found  → continue
```

Step 5 — Result
```
return true  →  "abaac" and "aacba" are Anagrams

